    "https://jobs.aum.edu/aum-careers-home": {
      "title": "WORKING AT AUBURN UNIVERSITY AT MONTGOMERY",
      "description": "AUM Careers Home Skip to Main Content Internal Candidates Returning Candidate Candidate Dashboard Manage Job Alerts Toggle navigation Careers Home Apply Process Search Jobs Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Student Jobs Internal Candidates Returning Candidate Candidate Dashboard Manage Job Alerts WORKING AT AUBURN UNIVERSITY AT MONTGOMERY Job Opportunities Our Work Changes Lives At Auburn University at Montgomery, we shape the future of Alabama, the nation, and the world through innovative education, life-changing research, and dedicated service. And we believe in investing in the employees who have made AUM one of the top universities in the region by expanding opportunities for a purposeful, rewarding life and career. Faculty Staff Students Experience Exceptional Benefits A career at AUM means a path to health and wellness, educational opportunities, a solid financial, future and time to enjoy those benefits. Health and Wellness Our comprehensive health insurance packages, along with wellness programs for employees and their families, ensure peace of mind and prioritize your well-being. Health, Dental and Vision Options Flexible Spending Account Employee Pharmacy Medical Leave Health Benefits Retirement All eligible Auburn University employees are enrolled in the Retirement Systems of Alabama. Additional voluntary retirement plans are available as well as retirement education to help employees build a solid financial future. Retirement Systems of Alabama Voluntary 403(b) and 457(b) Retirement Benefits More Advantages Benefits extend beyond health and retirement with education benefits for both employees and their dependents. Auburn also offers employees generous leave and holidays to encourage work/life balance. Employee Discounts Holidays Educational Opportunities More Benefits WHY AUM South’s Best Regional University AUM is consistently ranked among the South’s top regional universities for quality, value, and student success. Innovation at Work For eight consecutive years, readers of the Montgomery Advertiser have named AUM the River Region’s best. Our graduates deliver the skills, innovation, and leadership that strengthen industries and support employers. A Top Choice for Veterans Recognized by U.S. News & World Report as one of the South’s Best Colleges for Veterans, AUM provides dedicated support and resources to help service members, veterans, and their families succeed. Calling AUM Home Auburn University at Montgomery (AUM) is recognized by U.S. News and World Report, as well as, The Princeton Review as one of the best colleges in the Southeast. Explore AUM Explore Campus Working at AUM has been an awesome experience. As an HR professional, I am able to promote all the factors that have made AUM the best place to work, attract top talent, and foster professional development among our employees. It also brings me great joy to be employed at the university where I began my college career. Aundracus Stephens, MBA, M.Ed. HR Generalist II/III Office of Human Resources I enjoy working at AUM because I truly feel valued. Every day, I have the opportunity to work at an institution whose name speaks for itself. Collaborating with other talented people who are just as passionate about cultivating the best experience for its students, staff, and faculty is what I love about being an AUM Warhawk. Charlene Bell, M.A.Ed. HR Generalist II Office of Human Resources AUM has done so much for me over the past 22 years, both personally and professionally. Having earned three degrees here and now working toward my doctorate, it’s my privilege to give back. AUM has provided opportunities for growth; supported me through difficult times, and brought so much happiness and fulfillment to my life. AUM is family, and I love it! Amy Ingram, Ed. S. Director Experiential Education and Engagement Center What I love most about working at AUM is the students. Every day, I have the opportunity to encourage, support, and celebrate their growth, both academically and personally. Being part of a campus that truly values student success and community allows me to make a meaningful impact, and that’s what makes AUM a special place to work. Chanell Davis, Ph.D. Associate Director Warhawk Academic Success Center See jobs by: Categories Brands Locations Faculty and Staff Resources Privacy Policy Campus Map Public Safety/AUM Police Dept admissions@aum.edu 334-244-3000 A University In Motion 2026 All Rights Reserved. Auburn University at Montgomery. Privacy Policy . Cookies are used on this site to assist in continually improving the candidate experience and all the interaction data we store of our visitors is anonymous. Learn more about your rights on our Privacy Policy page. Okay x"
    },
